# Upstream: TikTok LIVE capture -> moderator -> TTLive (local runtime env)
# Copy to .env (gitignored; never commit secrets).
# Chain: TikTok LIVE --(bridge)--> moderator :3002 --(forward)--> TTLive :3001

# Target for bridge POSTs. Default points at the MODERATOR (not TTLive directly),
# so every event passes through moderation first. Moderator forwards clean
# events on to UPSTREAM_TTLIVE_URL.
TTLIVE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3002

# Must equal the moderator's API_TOKEN (fail-closed 401 on mismatch).
# Same value in moderator/.env. Generate:  py -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
API_TOKEN=changeme-generate-with-secrets-token_hex-32
TTLIVE_API_TOKEN=changeme-generate-with-secrets-token_hex-32

# Euler Stream signing key for production-grade WebSocket stability.
# Without it the free tier is severely rate-limited. Get one at eulerstream.com.
# TIKTOK_EULER_API_KEY=

# NOTE: prefer 127.0.0.1 over localhost on Windows (IPv6/DNS fallback stalls).
